<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Price substrate nightly on Basilic. PS-1B Phase D.

     Slot 21:00 local (Basilic = America/New_York), ruled by Mando 2026-09-02.

     This one DOES have an ordering dependency, unlike capex. Smart Money's
     22:30 scan will read the freshness ledger as a precondition once Phase 4
     lands, so the price store has to be current before it starts. Measured, the
     nightly append is ~9 minutes at v1 scope (516 names, 0.51 s/name over a
     short window) and the verification sweep is ~22 minutes at the 72 s pace
     floor, so a 21:00 start finishes near 21:35 and clears 22:30 with an hour
     to spare.

     The neighbour is com.abelard.news-watch at 21:30. BASILIC_MANUAL 13 records
     it as installed 2026-08-24; `launchctl list` on Basilic 2026-09-02 does not
     list it, so it is authored and not activated (E32, CR-R0 R4.3). Today there
     is nothing at 21:00-21:35 to collide with. If news-watch is ever loaded, a
     ~35-minute prices run overlaps its start by ~5 minutes — tolerable, since
     the two share no store and no writer and the overlapping leg is the last
     and least consequential one (verify), but it is the reason the legs are
     ordered as they are and not a coincidence to be re-derived later.

     RunAtLoad false: it fires on schedule, never on boot. A boot-time run would
     make a reboot indistinguishable from a real night in the logs — and the
     cold-start path has never been exercised (see OPERATIONS.md).

     ExitTimeOut 3600: the full night is ~35 minutes at v1 scope. Past an hour
     something is hanging — most likely a vendor not answering — and the run
     should die rather than still be holding the store when SM starts at 22:30.

     This file is the REFERENCE COPY kept in the repo. The live plist is
     host-specific and lives at ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.abelard.prices.plist.
     Only editing the plist needs a reload; a code change just needs git pull. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.abelard.prices</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>/Users/wafflehaus/Code/Abelard/daemons/common/scripts/run_prices.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>21</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>0</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/wafflehaus/Code/Abelard/daemons/common</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/wafflehaus/.openclaw/prices/logs/launchd.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/wafflehaus/.openclaw/prices/logs/launchd.err.log</string>
  <key>ExitTimeOut</key>
  <integer>3600</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
